#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007fcd15-219d-5a7b-979f-5872cbdb9291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} & \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{x}{y} & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430414} {:answer/id #uuid "157d76c9-2e6f-5cdb-897c-847f29e94391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{x}{y} & -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430417} {:answer/id #uuid "349923f1-1f51-5fc6-9589-ada6acd4c3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430423} {:answer/id #uuid "7529d158-9818-51d1-bf9e-38fc8f2bbd6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{x}{y} & -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430429} {:answer/id #uuid "ea727c2d-0baf-5e14-8734-e9b51371b264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} & -\\frac{x}{y}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "349923f1-1f51-5fc6-9589-ada6acd4c3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430423} :answer-field/id #uuid "eca99a2b-d50a-519b-aef0-e2b86f3c4cf7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98de8580-5081-5c82-af81-6826d2545a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-102461" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & \\frac{x}{y}-1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}-1)=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}-1)=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "376b6d35-c19b-56a0-93ca-9e64900695ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526607} {:answer/id #uuid "4d63a9d4-f48b-551f-a330-cb4773261398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526660} {:answer/id #uuid "57cd56c0-cc2d-5c47-9c19-0fd322aee1ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526683} {:answer/id #uuid "7f6fbe7f-9b92-59d9-8aed-d5539feec274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526755} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b9d20a-a2bf-5378-921c-e265c88f998e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f6fbe7f-9b92-59d9-8aed-d5539feec274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526755} :answer-field/id #uuid "905b588f-0f57-5923-a81f-afb037b87739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33021c77-54f7-572b-82bd-06940f46518d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102691" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{2}-2x & 2y{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{2}-2x & 2y{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}],$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{2}-2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}-2x)=2{y}^{2}-2\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y{x}^{2})=4xy \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}-2x)=4xy\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{x}^{2})=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-2 & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,-1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,-1)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,-1)=0\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-4)=-16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7ccfc6-c980-5f87-98b3-cb27c26de86d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281784} {:answer/id #uuid "1cc546d0-b0b6-5368-af23-5ec0c2c96352" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281949} {:answer/id #uuid "48389a8d-c104-542e-8686-3b973c39c4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282301} {:answer/id #uuid "7f03e21b-fba2-5b1e-bbaa-ba00d1112786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282783} {:answer/id #uuid "c372c923-e6e7-5ef4-8346-000c6e272e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f03e21b-fba2-5b1e-bbaa-ba00d1112786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282783} :answer-field/id #uuid "533cc9b6-1b67-5a24-ae39-2f81ecaf9c2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64116d30-10df-5392-b872-327ec4131913" :question/math-academy-id "q-163642" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}4xy-3{y}^{2} & 2{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{bmatrix},$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det(\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n$\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}4xy-3{y}^{2} & 2{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{bmatrix},$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=4xy-3{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}-6xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy-3{y}^{2})=4y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-6xy)=4x-6y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy-3{y}^{2})=4x-6y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-6xy)=-6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4y & 4x-6y \\\\ 4x-6y & -6x\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(1,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=4\\cdot (-6)-(-2)\\cdot (-2)=-28.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e80e6d5-e332-5afa-ba42-d5007ebeac81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy} \\\\ {e}^{xy} & {x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394107} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe3ac6a-5289-56c8-a43c-0dd50e90253b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(1+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(1+xy) & {x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394108} {:answer/id #uuid "f7148b5f-bb4e-5a46-9866-cb5115f7f7af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}+xy \\\\ {e}^{xy}+xy & {e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394109} {:answer/id #uuid "16fdd3db-9b55-566b-86dc-7e9f1644148e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(2+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(2+xy) & {y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394110} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1384d2-d73e-5e0f-90d8-1bd54737465e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(1+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(1+xy) & {e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebe3ac6a-5289-56c8-a43c-0dd50e90253b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(1+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(1+xy) & {x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394108} :answer-field/id #uuid "bab53cf7-593b-54ae-b653-6ab7353d6f02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b55b18c-139d-56b5-94eb-26aeb293ef39" :question/math-academy-id "q-80947" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}y{e}^{xy} & x{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{xy})={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{xy})={e}^{xy}+xy\\,\\text{ }{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})={e}^{xy}+xy\\,\\text{ }{e}^{xy}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{xy})={x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(1+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(1+xy) & {x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0379a8f3-5c08-5a0e-9aa9-ee7247f5bb7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2y & 2x \\\\ 2x & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348479} {:answer/id #uuid "0f2c18f5-f6c6-5cb7-9bd3-ef891a719882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348580} {:answer/id #uuid "235323a0-a480-5c75-9639-2308eb39664a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2y & 2xy \\\\ 2xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348748} {:answer/id #uuid "3438c329-ab2c-5701-840d-707e4cfa738f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2y \\\\ 2y & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348915} {:answer/id #uuid "703d071f-0017-59ad-ade4-9601ec2c639e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "703d071f-0017-59ad-ade4-9601ec2c639e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349481} :answer-field/id #uuid "1892be87-58b9-5f45-a8a1-451663b051c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "235e87ab-40f0-5bca-9e1d-4479ce5e2de8" :question/math-academy-id "q-81119" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)={y}^{2}({x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}({x}^{2}-1))\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{2} & 2y({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y({x}^{2}-1))=4xy \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2})=4xy\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y({x}^{2}-1))=2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
